# Generated by Claudian.
"""Labelled training data for the local intent classifier.

Maps utterance -> skill name.  Used by `training/train_intent_model.py`.

Why this exists
---------------
The router currently falls back to a Groq LLM call whenever no skill matches
by regex above 0.85 confidence.  That call costs 300-500ms *before any work
starts*, on every ambiguous utterance.  A small local model trained on this
data answers the same question in single-digit milliseconds.

Coverage notes
--------------
* Every skill in the registry has examples, including `conversation`, which
  is the catch-all and therefore needs the widest variety.
* Phrasings intentionally include the sloppy, clipped, and half-grammatical
  forms that speech-to-text actually produces — not tidy written English.
* Near-miss pairs are deliberate ("open docker" -> open_app vs "how do i use
  docker" -> coding_assistant) so the model learns the boundary rather than
  keying on a single word.
"""

